Package: google-chrome-synos
Version: ${UPSTREAM_VERSION}+synos1
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: ${ARCH}
Conflicts: google-chrome-stable
Replaces: google-chrome-stable
Maintainer: ${BRAND_VENDOR} <${BRAND_URL_SUPPORT}>
Homepage: ${BRAND_URL_HOME}
Description: Google Chrome, headless-capable, repackaged for ${BRAND_NAME}
 Repackaged from Google's own apt repository (dl.google.com), with the
 upstream maintainer scripts dropped: the real google-chrome-stable
 postinst registers its own apt source and a cron auto-updater, neither of
 which belongs on a built image. Ships /usr/bin/google-chrome-stable and
 nothing that registers it in a desktop menu — it exists to be driven
 headlessly over the Chrome DevTools Protocol (tools/devtools_browser.py),
 not opened by hand. Ubuntu's own "chromium"/"chromium-browser" package
 only installs the Chromium *snap*, which this engine's images never
 carry (bases/ubuntu/packages.map); this is the real fix for that gap.
